AUTHOR
FIREWHEEL Team
DONE
DESCRIPTION
Install a new repository of Model Components.
The repository should be an existing directory on the filesystem.
The path may be specified absolute or relative.
If the path does not exist, an error message is printed.

Some Model Components may provide additional installation details which can be executed to perform other setup steps (e.g., installing an extra Python package or downloading an external VM resource).
This takes the form of either an ``INSTALL`` directory with a ``vars.yml`` and a ``tasks.yml`` that are Ansible tasks which can be executed.
Alternatively, it can be a single ``INSTALL`` script that can be can be any executable file type as defined by a `shebang <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shebang_(Unix)>`_ line.

.. warning::

    The execution of Model Component ``INSTALL`` scripts can be a **DANGEROUS** operation.
    Please ensure that you **fully trust** the repository developer prior to executing these scripts.

.. seealso::

    See :ref:`mc_install` for more information on ``INSTALL`` scripts.

When installing a Model Component, users will have a variety of choices to select:

- ``y`` - yes, install execute this script
- ``n`` - no, do not execute this script
- ``v`` - view, see the script text
- ``vc`` - view color, see the script text with color support, must use a system pager which supports this behavior (e.g. ``PAGER='less -R'``)
- ``q`` - quit, exit immediately


Arguments
+++++++++

.. option:: path

    The path to the repository to install. If not provided, will assume that the user desires to run the installation scripts for all existing repositories (assuming the ``-s`` flag is also used).

.. option::  -s, --script

    Run any Model Component-specific installation scripts. The install script should be in the Model Components top-level directory in a file called ``INSTALL``.

.. option::  -i, --insecure

    Automatically run all Model Component INSTALL scripts. Must be run with the :option:`repository install -s` option to take effect.
    In this mode the INSTALL output is not shown on the terminal; it is saved to a log file for each Model Component, and the end of the log for any failed Model Component is shown in the final summary.

.. option::  -f, --fail-fast

    Stop at the first Model Component INSTALL that fails, rather than continuing with the remaining Model Components.
    Must be run with the :option:`repository install -s` option to take effect.

.. option:: -h, --help

    Show a help message and exit.


Examples
++++++++

``firewheel repository install <directory>``

``firewheel repository install --script <directory>``

``firewheel repository install --script --insecure --fail-fast``

When INSTALL scripts are run, a summary is printed at the end listing every Model Component that has an INSTALL, its outcome, and the path of the log containing its output.
The command exits with a non-zero code if any INSTALL failed.

DONE
RUN LocalPython ON control
#!/usr/bin/env python

import sys
import time
import argparse
from pathlib import Path

from rich.text import Text
from rich.table import Table, Column
from rich.console import Console
from rich.progress import Progress, TextColumn

from firewheel.control.repository_db import RepositoryDb
from firewheel.control.model_component_install import (
    InstallStatus,
    ModelComponentInstall,
)
from firewheel.control.model_component_iterator import ModelComponentIterator

LOG_TAIL_LINES = 20

STATUS_STYLES = {
    InstallStatus.INSTALLED: "green",
    InstallStatus.ALREADY_INSTALLED: "green",
    InstallStatus.SKIPPED: "yellow",
    InstallStatus.FAILED: "b red",
}


def install_repo(repo):
    """
    Install the given FIREWHEEL repository.

    Args:
        repo (dict): A dictionary object which can be added as a new FIREWHEEL repository.
    """
    repo_db = RepositoryDb()
    ret = repo_db.add_repository(repo)
    if ret:
        Console().print("[green]Repository successfully installed!")
    else:
        Console().print("[yellow]Duplicate repositories cannot be installed!")


def run_install_scripts(repos, insecure=False, fail_fast=False):
    """
    Ask the user to run the install script for all the Model Components
    of the provided repositories.

    Args:
        repos (list): Repository dictionaries whose Model Components should be installed.
        insecure (bool): Whether to automatically install all Model Components without asking
            for each one. This also hides the INSTALL output on the terminal.
        fail_fast (bool): Whether to stop after the first Model Component that fails.

    Returns:
        list: A ``(mc_name, repo_path, status, log_path)`` tuple for each Model Component
        that has an INSTALL.
    """
    results = []
    for repo in repos:
        for mc in ModelComponentIterator(iter([repo])):
            mci = ModelComponentInstall(mc, quiet=insecure)
            mci.run_install_script(insecure=insecure)
            if mci.status is None:
                # The Model Component has no INSTALL.
                continue
            results.append((mc.name, repo["path"], mci.status, mci.log_path))
            if fail_fast and mci.status is InstallStatus.FAILED:
                return results
    return results


def read_log_tail(log_path, num_lines=LOG_TAIL_LINES):
    """
    Read the last lines of a log file.

    Args:
        log_path (pathlib.Path): The log file to read.
        num_lines (int): The number of lines to return.

    Returns:
        str: The last ``num_lines`` lines of the file, or :py:data:`None` if it is
        unreadable.
    """
    try:
        text = Path(log_path).read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
    except OSError:
        return None
    return "\n".join(text.splitlines()[-num_lines:])


def print_summary(results, fail_fast=False):
    """
    Print the outcome of every attempted Model Component INSTALL.

    The end of the log for each failure is printed first, followed by a table of all
    results, so that the failures are the last thing on the screen rather than buried
    in the INSTALL output.

    Args:
        results (list): The results from :py:func:`run_install_scripts`.
        fail_fast (bool): Whether the run stopped at the first failure.

    Returns:
        bool: :py:data:`True` if no Model Component failed to install,
        :py:data:`False` otherwise.
    """
    console = Console()
    failed = [result for result in results if result[2] is InstallStatus.FAILED]

    for name, _repo_path, _status, log_path in failed:
        tail = read_log_tail(log_path) if log_path else None
        if tail is None:
            continue
        console.rule(f"[b red]Last {LOG_TAIL_LINES} lines of output for {name}")
        console.print(Text.from_ansi(tail))

    if results:
        table = Table(title="Model Component INSTALL Summary")
        table.add_column("Model Component", style="cyan")
        table.add_column("Repository")
        table.add_column("Status")
        table.add_column("Log", overflow="fold")
        # Show failures last, so they are closest to the prompt.
        for name, repo_path, status, log_path in sorted(
            results, key=lambda result: result[2] is InstallStatus.FAILED
        ):
            table.add_row(
                name,
                repo_path,
                f"[{STATUS_STYLES[status]}]{status.value}",
                str(log_path) if log_path else "",
            )
        console.print(table)

    if failed:
        console.print(
            f"[b red]{len(failed)} of {len(results)} Model Component INSTALLs failed: "
            f"{', '.join(result[0] for result in failed)}"
        )
        if fail_fast:
            console.print("[b red]Stopped after the first failure (--fail-fast).")
        return False

    console.print("[green]All Model Components were installed or skipped!")
    return True


if __name__ == "__main__":
    con = Console()
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description="Install a new model component repository!"
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--script",
        "-s",
        required=False,
        action="store_true",
        dest="script",
        help=str(
            "Run any Model Component-specific installation scripts. "
            "The install script should be in the Model Components top-level directory in a "
            "file called `INSTALL`."
        ),
        default=False,
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--insecure",
        "-i",
        required=False,
        action="store_true",
        help=str(
            "Automatically run all Model Component INSTALL scripts. "
            "Must be run with the '-s/--script' option to take effect."
        ),
        default=False,
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--fail-fast",
        "-f",
        required=False,
        action="store_true",
        dest="fail_fast",
        help=str(
            "Stop at the first Model Component INSTALL that fails. "
            "Must be run with the '-s/--script' option to take effect."
        ),
        default=False,
    )
    parser.add_argument("path", help="The path to the repository to install.", nargs="?")

    args = parser.parse_args()

    if args.path is None and not args.script:
        parser.error("a path is required unless --script is given")

    PATH = None
    REPO_ENTRY = None
    if args.path:
        PATH = Path(args.path)
        REPO_ENTRY = {"path": str(PATH.resolve())}

    SUCCESS = True

    if args.script:
        con.print(
            "[yellow]Running any Model Component install scripts. This could be "
            "a [red]DANGEROUS[/red] operation!!! "
            "[yellow]Ensure that you completely trust the Model Component "
            "creator before continuing!"
        )
        if args.insecure:
            DESCRIPTION = str(
                "[b red]You used INSECURE mode. This will automatically run "
                "all Model Component install scripts. Pausing for: "
            )
            text_column = TextColumn(  # noqa: FS003
                (
                    "[progress.description]{task.description}"  # noqa: FS003
                    "[cyan]{task.remaining}[/cyan] seconds."  # noqa: FS003
                ),
                table_column=Column(ratio=1),
            )
            progress = Progress(text_column, expand=True)

            with progress as p:
                task = p.add_task(DESCRIPTION, total=10)
                for _ in range(10):
                    p.update(task, advance=1, refresh=True)
                    time.sleep(1)
            con.print("[green]Continuing...")  # noqa: FS003

        REPOS = RepositoryDb().list_repositories() if PATH is None else [REPO_ENTRY]
        RESULTS = run_install_scripts(REPOS, args.insecure, args.fail_fast)
        SUCCESS = print_summary(RESULTS, args.fail_fast)

    if PATH is not None and SUCCESS:
        install_repo(REPO_ENTRY)

    sys.exit(0 if SUCCESS else 1)
DONE
